{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2879,
    "dDurationMs": 5010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The universe as a whole evolves towards increasing\nentropy, or disorder -- a tendency physicists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7889,
    "dDurationMs": 2071,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "call the Second Law of Thermodynamics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This movement toward disorganization might\nlead you to think that organized structures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14440,
    "dDurationMs": 4589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– like, say, living beings – would never\nspontaneously come into existence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19029,
    "dDurationMs": 4352,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course entropy can go down in part of the\nuniverse -- you can trade a decrease in entropy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23381,
    "dDurationMs": 5079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in one place (like cooling water so it crystallizes\ninto ice) for an equal or larger increase"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28460,
    "dDurationMs": 3209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in entropy somewhere else (like heating the\nback of your fridge)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31669,
    "dDurationMs": 3671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Order increases here, but only at the cost\nof decreasing order there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35340,
    "dDurationMs": 5030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we can still ask: why do intricate, complex\nstructures come into being in the universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40370,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if the overall tendency is toward increasing\ndisorder?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43700,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The secret is that order and complexity are\nvery different ideas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48070,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Entropy measures how many different ways you\ncan make an arrangement of small-scale particles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52210,
    "dDurationMs": 5050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that have the same large-scale properties:\nlike, 37 degrees celsius, brown hair, good"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57260,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at soccer, and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58460,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[There are lots of different ways!]."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60110,
    "dDurationMs": 4830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Complexity, on the other hand, is a measure\nof how hard it is to describe a set of large-scale"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64940,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "properties."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65940,
    "dDurationMs": 4359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Simple systems are easy to describe; complex\nsystems require a lot more information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70299,
    "dDurationMs": 2871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, take a cup filled with half coffee\nand half milk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73170,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It starts off in a state with relatively low\nentropy – you could swap coffee molecules"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77130,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with each other, or milk molecules with each\nother, without changing things substantially."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81200,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you swapped coffee molecules with milk\nmolecules that would be a noticeable change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85600,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s also a simple setup -- milk on top,\ncoffee on the bottom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88850,
    "dDurationMs": 5369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, as the milk and coffee begin to mix,\nentropy goes up – where they are mixed together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94219,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "swapping some coffee molecules for milk molecules\nno longer makes much of a difference."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98539,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the system also becomes more complex - to\ndescribe what you see, you would have to specify"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102889,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exactly how all of those tendrils of milk\nand coffee intricately swirl into each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108229,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Continuing on, entropy keeps going up, until\nthe milk and coffee are completely mixed together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112659,
    "dDurationMs": 3491,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and swapping any molecules of coffee and milk\nwith any others doesn’t really make any"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116150,
    "dDurationMs": 1239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "difference at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117389,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s equilibrium, where there are a huge\nnumber of arrangements of the molecules that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120889,
    "dDurationMs": 1561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "look essentially the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122450,
    "dDurationMs": 4659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this highly-mixed equilibrium is once\nagain simple: it’s just a homogenous mixture"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127109,
    "dDurationMs": 3831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of coffee and milk; no more complicated fractal\nswirly stuff."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130940,
    "dDurationMs": 4761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This general principle is borne out time and\ntime again: while entropy increases, complexity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135701,
    "dDurationMs": 2939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "initially grows, then decays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138640,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Complexity can be a natural step along the\npath to increasing entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142170,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The best example is the universe itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143920,
    "dDurationMs": 5530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The early universe was very smooth and very\ndense: that’s low-entropy, and also extremely simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149680,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The far future will be smooth again, but very\ndilute: that’s high-entropy, and again extremely simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155120,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s now, in the medium-entropy middle,\nthat things look complex."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159130,
    "dDurationMs": 4850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stars and galaxies and veins of minerals in\nrock and swirling clouds and amino acids and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163980,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "proteins and human beings and cats – we’re\nat the exciting, beautiful stage of the coffee"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169180,
    "dDurationMs": 600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mixing!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169920,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But just as with the coffee and milk, in the\nfar distant future complexity will decrease"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174830,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "again, and complicated stuff like us will\nat last be simplified out of existence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184680,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, Henry here, thanks for watching."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186870,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the third video in a series about\ntime and entropy made in collaboration with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190510,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physicist Sean Carroll."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191950,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The series is supported with funding from\nGoogle’s Making and Science initiative,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195590,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which seeks to encourage more young people\n(and people of all ages) to learn about and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199220,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fall in love with science and the world around\nthem, and the videos are based off of Sean’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203010,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "book “The Big Picture: On the Origins of\nLife, Meaning, and the Universe Itself,”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206880,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which you can find online or in bookstores\naround the world."
    } ]
  } ]
}
